# Lore drafts (canon: soft): the academy and its customs.

@lore lumenhold
keys: Lumenhold, academy, seven towers, bridges of light
canon: soft
text: Lumenhold Academy is seven towers joined by bridges of light, standing above a mirror-still lake. It has trained mages for three hundred years and has been a seal for exactly as long.

@lore mirror_lake
keys: Mirror Lake, lake
canon: soft
text: The lake is so still it shows the towers upside down. Students swim in it in summer and catch Lake Fever when they shouldn't. Some nights it calls to seers.

@lore houses
keys: houses, Emberhall, Rootward, Stillwater, Duskgate, Brasswick
canon: soft
text: Students belong to five houses: Emberhall (fire and ambition), Rootward (growing things), Stillwater (quiet and the far-sighted), Duskgate (shadows and secrets) and Brasswick (makers and tinkerers). Faculty belong to none.

@lore crowns
keys: crowns, money, currency
canon: soft
text: The currency is the crown. Rent and board at the academy cost about ten crowns a month; a good meal in the village, one; a registered familiar, twenty.

@lore calendar
keys: Harvestmoon, Emberwane, Mistveil, Frostcall, Deepwinter, Thawmoon, Stormbloom, Greenrise, Blossomtide, Highsun, Goldenhaze, Starfall
canon: soft
text: The academic year starts in autumn with Harvestmoon, then Emberwane, Mistveil, Frostcall, Deepwinter, Thawmoon, Stormbloom, Greenrise, Blossomtide, Highsun, Goldenhaze and Starfall.

@lore festivals
keys: Harvest Feast, Lantern Night, Midwinter Ball, Spring Tournament, Starfall festival
canon: soft
text: The Harvest Feast opens the year; on Lantern Night lanterns carry wishes over the lake; the Midwinter Ball fills the Great Hall; the Spring Tournament crowns a duelling champion; and at Starfall the whole academy sleeps on the lawns to watch the meteors.

@lore exams
keys: Winter Trials, Grand Examinations, exams
canon: soft
text: The Winter Trials test the term's work in Frostcall. The Grand Examinations close the year: three days, five examiners and a practical before a panel that includes the headmistress.

@lore restricted_section
keys: Restricted Section, silver key
canon: soft
text: A locked section at the back of the library, opened by a silver key, where black-bound books breathe softly. Bartholomew the goat once ate a third of "Curses of the Northern Wastes" there.

@lore confiscation_vault
keys: confiscation vault, contraband
canon: soft
text: Three hundred years of everything the faculty ever took off a student. Its alarm is a very loud goblin.

@lore gargoyles
keys: gargoyle, third gargoyle, passages
canon: soft
text: The castle is riddled with passages that appear on no official plan. The way into the Midnight Cartographers' world is behind the third gargoyle on the north parapet.

@lore moving_stairs
keys: staircases, moving stairs, east wing
canon: soft
text: Lumenhold's staircases move when they feel like it and occasionally eat shoes, which turn up under the stairs in the east wing.

@lore demerits
keys: demerits, prefects, detention, sash
canon: soft
text: Prefects wear red sashes and keep ledgers of demerits. Detention is usually scrubbing pans or cataloguing contraband. Being stripped of a sash is the worst thing that can happen to a prefect short of expulsion.

@lore familiars
keys: familiars, registration, Ember
canon: soft
text: Students may keep a familiar if it is registered: twenty crowns and a stamp from the registrar. Unregistered familiars are tolerated if nobody notices them, and some don't want to be noticed.

@lore lumen_ledger
keys: Lumen Ledger, newspaper, press
canon: soft
text: The student newspaper, printed at dawn on a press that groans like a dragon. Its gossip column is feared; its editor, Nessa Quill, has a quill that writes on its own.

@lore infirmary
keys: infirmary, Sister Amaranth, Lake Fever
canon: soft
text: Sister Amaranth runs the infirmary with warming charms, tonics and no patience for excuses. Lake Fever comes from swimming where you shouldn't; curse-cold comes from worse.

@lore graduation
keys: graduation, speech, yearbook
canon: soft
text: Each year one graduate speaks for their class in the Great Hall, chosen by the faculty. Graduates plant something, keep something, or leave something behind.

@lore fairs
keys: Club Fair, Job Board, Artificers' Fair, Midsummer Fair
canon: soft
text: In Emberwane the Club Fair fills the courtyard with recruiting tables; the Job Board in the entrance hall posts term-time work. The Artificers' Fair shows off students' machines, and in summer the village holds its Midsummer Fair with an enchanted carousel.

@lore disciplinary_board
keys: Disciplinary Board, probation, expulsion
canon: soft
text: When a student's standing collapses, the Disciplinary Board meets: three professors, a long table and very little mercy. Probation comes first; expulsion second.

@lore lumen_essay_prize
keys: Lumen Essay Prize, essay prize
canon: soft
text: An annual prize of thirty crowns for the best student essay on a set theme, judged by the faculty. Past themes include "Magic and Duty".

@lore sorting_mirror
keys: Sorting Mirror, entrance hall
canon: soft
text: A tall enchanted mirror in the entrance hall. It does not sort anyone into anything; it asks, in a voice like cold water, who you were before you came.

@lore spire_library
keys: Spire Library, the Spire
canon: soft
text: The academy's research library at the top of the tallest tower, where theses of distinction are shelved in a section students whisper about.

@lore the_season
keys: Season, the Season, patrons
canon: soft
text: The academy's patrons keep a Season: a round of suppers in their town houses in the village below the hill, closed by the patrons' ball. Students the castle is talking about are sometimes sent a card with a crest. It is an honour, and an inspection.

@lore brightwater
keys: Brightwater
canon: soft
text: A cloudy gold elixir from the village's back rooms, banned at Lumenhold. A dose keeps the body rested and the spirits high for weeks; the weeks after can drag. Grisk deals it.

@lore owls_ink
keys: Owl's Ink, owls ink
canon: soft
text: A bitter black elixir, banned at Lumenhold, that fills a tired student with magic and sharpens the mind like a new nib. Before finals it is worth more than gold; afterwards, for a while, nothing reads right. Grisk deals it, and before finals so do some of the older students.

@lore master_map
keys: Master Map, Keeper of the Map, Cartographer
canon: soft
text: The Midnight Cartographers' Master Map: a great sheet of silver ink that shifts as the castle does. A Keeper looks after it and hands the keeping on when the club decides. For thirty years it had two great blanks: the stair below the Restricted Section's chained shelf, and a stair inside the seventh tower's wall.
